    [Doc][BugFix] Scope MiniMax-M3 TOC depth and enable SSD LRU eviction (#19464)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Restore the original site-wide `toc_depth: 3`: deeper global settings
    also change unrelated model guides. Add a comment beside the setting
    warning against changing it for one model. A page-scoped hook rebuilds
    only MiniMax-M3's TOC at depth 4, so Sections 5.3.1/5.3.2 and
    5.4.1/5.4.2 remain visible while deeper headings stay out of the
    sidebar. The hook copies the Markdown extension configuration and leaves
    the rendered HTML and shared configuration unchanged.
    
    Also add `MOONCAKE_OFFLOAD_BUCKET_EVICTION_POLICY=lru` immediately below
    the two SSD capacity exports in the common pooling block and all four
    A3/950DT Prefill/Decode templates. Briefly explain least-recently-used
    eviction; the default `none` policy rejects new writes when the bucket
    fills.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation and TOC presentation only. Other guides return to the
    original depth of 3, while MiniMax-M3 alone displays fourth-level
    headings. Chapter structure, heading anchors, navigation entries, and
    runtime implementation are unchanged.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Full MkDocs builds passed for main and v0.30. Compared all 55 main /
    54 release model pages: heading anchors are unchanged; all other model
    TOCs match their prior entries filtered to depth 3; MiniMax-M3 matches
    depth 4 and includes 5.3.1, 5.3.2, 5.4.1, and 5.4.2.
    - Verified that the hook returns the rendered HTML unchanged, does not
    mutate shared extension configuration, and leaves another model page's
    TOC untouched.
    - codespell, typos, Ruff checks/formatting, and `git diff --check`
    passed. Earlier Markdown checks and all five changed pooling Bash blocks
    also passed; the three SSD exports appear consecutively in the requested
    order.
    - `bash format.sh ci` was attempted but timed out installing
    actionlint/pre-commit dependencies; focused checks passed. No NPU
    runtime test or permanent tests were added.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
